          "heading": "Expert FAQ Stack",
          "faqs": [
            {
              "q": "What defines the core advantage of a multi-franchise commercial truck dealer?",
              "a": "A multi-franchise footprint permits our dealership to provide neutral, application-specific vehicle evaluations, drawing matching equipment directly from premier brands like Volvo, Western Star, Autocar, and BYD to suit your precise corporate needs."
            },
            {
              "q": "How does family-owned management impact post-sale service delivery?",
              "a": "Family ownership ensures client accounts retain immediate access to executive decision-makers, bypassing the rigid, multi-layered approvals common in corporate groups to provide flexible financing, service scheduling, and emergency logistics tracking."
            },
            {
              "q": "What total capacity does the Secaucus complex maintain?",
              "a": "Our 100,000 square-foot facility accommodates 32 advanced service bays, a multi-million dollar parts store, 26 service technicians, 16 tracked parts delivery vehicles, and a dedicated field staff managing 4 mobile emergency service trucks."
            },
            {
              "q": "How does Hudson County Motors support green-energy fleet transitions?",
              "a": "As the state’s first certified Volvo EV truck center, we supply complete vehicle procurement, charging layout mapping, and factory-certified high-voltage diagnostic and repair support for electric models like the BYD-8TT."
            },
            {
              "q": "What vocational sectors does your customized upfitting department support?",
              "a": "We collaborate with premium body upfitters to deliver custom severe-duty trucks, including construction dump vehicles, garbage rear/side loaders, industrial hook lifts, concrete mixers, and specialized crane equipment."
            }
          ]
        },
